pub const CONTENT: &str = "Workspace memory is durable OKF v0.3 Markdown knowledge that the harness maintains. Relevant concepts reach the request automatically as untrusted references; verify a recalled fact against live files before relying on it, and do not search memory yourself. When the primary task is complete and validated, record each newly verified, durable, non-obvious fact, decision, constraint, preference, lesson, troubleshooting finding, procedure, or known issue once with the memory tool: call template for its canonical shape, cite the evidence in sources with matching footnotes, and write it. A near-duplicate answers duplicateOf; update that concept with its current digest instead. Retire outdated knowledge with supersede or retire. Never write generated or verified fields, and set status or stale_after only from evidence; the harness records authorship, derives trust, and rejects invented verification or human actors. Memory holds durable verified knowledge only: procedures belong in skills, events in session history, and behavior in harness configuration. Never store transient task state, transcripts, logs, secrets, credentials, personal data, private URLs, machine-local paths, or speculation. Do not interrupt the primary task to maintain memory.";
